B=r'''<style>.box p,.box li{font-size:17.5px;line-height:1.25}.box h2{font-size:22px;margin-bottom:3px}.code{font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.28}.tbl{font-size:15.5px}.tbl th,.tbl td{padding:2px 5px}.iq ol{font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.24}.pill{font-size:13px}.grid{gap:8px}.handle{bottom:-12px}.box{padding:8px 10px}.tagline{font-size:17px;margin-bottom:6px}.note{font-size:14.5px}</style>
<div class="title">🔬 HxGN EAM Calibrations <span class="badge">CHEAT SHEET</span></div>
<div class="tagline">Compare a device reading under a known standard load across test points — then prove it on Work Orders. (HxGN EAM Calibrations 12.3 brief)</div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="box c1"><h2>1. What &amp; why</h2><ul><li>Calibration = test unknown reading vs a <b>known standard</b></li><li>Need points across the full operating range (test points)</li><li>Regulated industries: pharma, oil/gas, food, automotive</li><li>Base EAM product — devices, standards, PM, WO results</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c2"><h2>2. Core objects</h2><ul><li><b>Devices</b> = Equipment (asset / position / system)</li><li><b>Standards</b> = Parts with Calibration Standard checkbox (or asset Parts)</li><li><b>Results</b> documented on Work Orders</li><li><b>Frequency</b> via PM Schedules / Maintenance Patterns</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c3"><h2>3. Equipment setup</h2><ul><li><b>Calibration</b> tab: tolerances, precision, increment, ranges, Default Set, SOP</li><li><b>Test Points</b> tab: Set + Sequence = PK (Sequence 0–9999)</li><li>Set groups weekly / monthly / annual point lists</li><li>Some fields default from device; blank TP uses device-level on WO</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c4"><h2>4. Categories &amp; generate</h2><ul><li>Categories = attribute templates (Calibration + Test Points tabs)</li><li>New Equipment with Category → copies cal data once at create</li><li>Update Equipment / Update Equipment Configurations cascade later changes</li><li>Equipment Configurations + <b>Generate Equipment</b> = batch devices</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c5"><h2>5. Standards Used</h2><ul><li>Tick <b>Calibration Standard</b> on the Part</li><li>Associate on Equipment → Parts Associated</li><li>On WO Calibration tab: <b>Standards Used</b> popup</li><li>Flagged parts copy to the WO; technician can adjust / pick asset</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c6"><h2>6. Process Loops</h2><ul><li>Loop = group calibrated together, not device-by-device</li><li>Loop Equipment: Loop checkbox + owns the test points</li><li>Input instrument: Type = <b>Standard applied to</b></li><li>Output instrument: Type = <b>Reading taken from</b></li><li>WO header = loop; each TP equipment = reading-taken-from</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c7"><h2>7. WO Type = Calibration</h2><ul><li>Copies device header + test points to WO Calibration tab</li><li>Also via Standard WO, PM, Patterns, Alerts, Flex rules</li><li>PM: set <b>Test Point Set</b> + Calibrations WO Type (else no copy)</li><li>As Found → optional Copy to As Left after adjust</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c8"><h2>8. Precision (v12.0+)</h2><table class="tbl"><tr><th>Param</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td><b>CALTZERO=A</b></td><td>auto trailing zeros to match precision</td></tr><tr><td><b>CALTZERO=B</b></td><td>only user-entered trailing zeros kept</td></tr><tr><td><b>CALTZERO=C</b></td><td>exact decimals required (+ CALRPREC)</td></tr><tr><td><b>CALPREC</b></td><td>ON/OFF precision on Output (etc.)</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="box c1" style="grid-column:1 / span 2"><h2>9. Status &amp; reports</h2><ul><li><b>Calibration Status</b> (calculated): Incomplete · Pass · Pass – Recal Exists · Pass – Fail Exists · Fail</li><li>Test point Status: Pass / Fail / Recal (Alert Tolerance band → Recal)</li><li>Reports: Due · Equipment · History · Record · Reverse Traceability · Analysis</li></ul></div>
<div class="bottom">
<div class="box" style="border-color:#1a5f7a"><h2 style="color:#1a5f7a">10a. Flow</h2><div class="flow" style="flex-wrap:wrap;row-gap:4px"><span class="pill">Equip + TPs</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Standards</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">PM / Type=Cal</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">WO Calibration</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Status + Reports</span></div></div>
<div class="box iq"><h2>10b. Consultant tips</h2><ol><li>Decide CALTZERO before go-live data entry</li><li>Use Sets for multi-frequency PM</li><li>Always set Calibrations WO Type on PM</li><li>Reverse Traceability for standard recalls</li></ol></div>
<div class="box" style="border-color:#2d8a5a"><h2 style="color:#2d8a5a">10c. Key points</h2><ul><li>Set+Seq = PK</li><li>Type=Calibration copies</li><li>Status is calculated</li></ul></div>
</div></div>'''
build("/workspace/social/posts/2026-10-17-linkedin-eam-calibrations",B,1350,"Rahul Kumar")
